    "description": "Develop tools to analyze energy usage data recorded by electric smart meters in real homes. Data set\nis noisy, sparse, and has multiple, potentially unknown, signal contributors. Written in Python.\n​* Wavelet Transform and Inverse Wavelet Transform - Perform time-frequency analysis to describe the\nenergy signatures of different electrical appliances.\n* Hidden Markov Model - Simulate the energy consumption pattern of electrical appliances using a\nHidden Markov chain. Parameters are trained via bayesian inference and the forward-backward\nalgorithm.\n* Feature-based disaggregator - Reduce each known appliance to a feature vector, and use Decision\nTrees to estimate the contributions of each appliance in the aggregate data.",
